name 'ai-and-algorithmic-decisions-postassessment-q10_2026'

question 'A login form changes its border color from gray to red when an entered password is too short. A user with low vision says the red is hard to see and they don''t know what changed. Which POUR principle is this design failing?'
wrong 'Robust — it does not work across browsers.'

right 'Perceivable — the user cannot notice the change because color alone is the only signal.'
wrong 'Operable — the form cannot be filled out.'
wrong 'Understandable — the form has too many fields.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 7
MARKDOWN
